 the evidence points to a comfortable incumbent win.", "watch": "Any late-arriving polling showing Jenkins within single digits, or a sudden influx of Republican outside spending into the district, would be the first sign this race deserves a second look.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Sharice Davids (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Sharice Davids, the Democratic incumbent, seeks another term in the Kansas City-area district, which leans slightly Democratic. She faces Republican Eric Jenkins, who has raised about $52,000, and Libertarian Steven Hohe. Davids has raised roughly $4.7 million and holds $1.9 million on hand, giving her an overwhelming financial edge. No independent public polls are available for the general election.\n\nEvery major race rater, from the Cook Political Report to the Economist, places the district in the Safe or Solid Democratic column, and prediction markets price her chances around 95 percent. The national political environment favors Democrats this cycle, adding to the incumbent's structural advantages. With a low-funded challenger, no reported outside spending, and a well-established incumbent focused on kitchen-table issues, the race has drawn little national attention and appears unlikely to be closely contested.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9826, "margin": 15.09}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9781, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.979, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.97, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9714, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9748, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9784, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9769, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9798, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9747, "margin":